  "query_preview": "(This evening through Thursday)...\nIssued at 230 PM EDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Tonight...\n\nThe current round of forcing is producing light rain across much of \ncentral Indiana this afternoon. Continued likely PoPs most areas as \nthis rain moves through. \n2\nWith the northern part of an upper trough axis still moving in, \nadditional showers may develop later this afternoon, so kept PoPs \ngoing most areas before 00Z. An isolated thunderstorm is possible, \nbut generally just showers are expected.\n\nThe upper trough will weaken this evening, but there looks to be \nenough forcing to continue PoPs across the southern half of the area \nthrough the evening. \n\nPatchy fog will develop tonight thanks to the continued moist \natmosphere and light winds. With clouds hanging around, widespread \nfog is not currently expected.\n\nLows tonight will be in the upper 50s north to middle 60s south.\n\nFriday and Saturday...\n\nSurface high pressure will keep much of the area dry through the day \nFriday. Friday night into Saturday, a weak upper trough will drift \nnortheast across the area. Moisture will increase as the upper \ntrough moves through. \n\nForcing from the trough will bring some scattered to perhaps \nnumerous showers to the area, especially south and east where the \nbetter forcing will be. Will go with mainly chance Pops (as best \nforcing will be east of the area), with perhaps some low likely PoPs \nin the far east.\n\nHighs on Friday will be mainly in the lower 80s. If rain coverage \nremains low enough, highs on Saturday may reach the middle to upper \n80s. \n\nSunday and Monday...\n\nThe persistent upper ridge will attempt to sneak back into the area. \nBefore it does, some upper impulses may generate isolated convection \non Sunday, but confidence is low. \n\nHigh temperatures will depend on how far the ridge gets into the \narea. Highs near 90 are possible where the ridge rules, with 80s \nelsewhere. The most likely locations to see near 90 will be areas in \nthe southwest forecast area. Guidance continues to waffle though on \nthe higher temperatures, so confidence remains low to medium.\n\nTuesday and beyond...\n\nLarger upper troughing developing across the northern part of the \ncountry will bring a cold front into the area Tuesday into Thursday. \nThe front looks to slow down as it encounters the upper ridge, but \nhow far south it gets depends on how far north the ridge's influence \nextends. \n\nFor now will broadbrush mainly chance PoPs Tuesday afternoon into \nThursday. \n\nTemperatures around 90 may be able to be advected into most areas \nahead of the front on Tuesday, before the front and potential \nclouds/rain keep readings in the 80s for Wednesday and Thursday.",
